{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Which part of the brain, located inside the temporal lobe, is associated with memory formation?","hippocampus"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"science-technology\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["This evolutionary theory, proposed by the inimitable Stephen J. Gould and Niles Eldridge, argues that evolution occurs not gradually but rapidly after periods of stasis and in isolated, localized areas.","Punctuated Equilibrium"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"science-technology\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["This three million year old skeleton known as “Lucy” was discovered in 1974 and is almost 40% complete. Lucy was a small, chimp-like hominid but walked upright like modern humans. She is a member of this species.","Australopithecus Afarensis"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"science-technology\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is the total collection of traits that determine the physical and behavioral aspects of an organism called?","Phenotype"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"science-technology\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["In 1912, a jawbone and fragments of a skull were discovered and originally named “dawn-man”. It wasn’t until 41 years later that it was exposed as a hoax. This darling of creationist skepticism is known as what?","Piltdown Man"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"science-technology\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Prior to Darwin’s theory, the most influential line of thought regarding the variety of life forms was a creationist doctrine that likened the biological functions in an organism to the intricate workings of a watch. Which Christian apologist put forth the “Watchmaker Analogy?","William Paley"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"science-technology\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["The evolutionary process where beneficial inherited traits become more prevalent in the succeeding generations of organisms, and unfavorable ones less common, is called what?","Natural Selection"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"science-technology\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["This monastic egghead pioneered the study of genetics, which eventually explained the mechanisms of speciation through genetic mutation. Who is the “father of modern genetics?”","Gregor Mendel"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"science-technology\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["The “peppered moth” is a prime example of micro evolution, where the moth’s color changed over a span of 200 years to match the soot-darkened trunks of the trees it inhabits. The darker moths survived because they were less conspicuous than their white counterparts to the birds that preyed on them. What is the term associated with the coloration change demonstrated in the peppered moth?","Industrial Melanism"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"science-technology\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["This animals evolutionary lineage is the best documented and the most clearly understood.","Horse"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"science-technology\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["During his famous voyage to the Galapagos Islands, Charles Darwin studied differences in a specific animal’s anatomy, his observations setting the stage for his eventual theory of evolution. What animal’s anatomy did Darwin study?","Finch beaks"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"science-technology\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
